# t0938 — COMPILER ICE. Moving a `Callable` local with the ratified `^` sigil
# (D27) into a consuming position panics the compiler at
# src/ir/lowering/mod.rs:2144 with "Tier 2a consume-site violation ... untracked
# source consumed". These are ratified consuming positions, so this is legal
# source answered with a crash.
#
# TWO CELLS, both `gg check`-clean, each with its OWN validator arm — the second
# was added 2026-09-02 after measuring that this is a CLASS, not one site:
#   1. `Some(^h)`             -> EnumInit(Some, arg #0)
#   2. `Vector[Callable].push(^h)` -> CollectionMutator(Vector__…__push, arg #1)
#
# ⚠ THE ENUMERATION IS TOTAL AND THREE SIBLINGS ARE GREEN, which is what makes a
# fix aimed at one arm suspect. Measured 2026-09-02, same `^h` on the same local:
#   `Dict[String, Callable].put("k", ^h)` -> builds, prints, rc 0
#   `Holder(^h)` struct-init              -> builds, prints 41, rc 0
#   `return ^h`                           -> builds, prints 41, rc 0
# Dict `put` is a CollectionMutator TOO and it is accepted, so the discriminator
# is NOT the position class — it is how the argument's ownership is tracked at
# these two arms. Fix the class (Core #4); do not patch the arm that panicked.
#
# INTENDED: prints 2 then 2 (or, if the move is to be refused, a DIAGNOSTIC —
# never a panic). The file ICEs on cell 1 today, so cell 2 is not yet observable;
# it is wired here so the net covers both cells the moment either is fixed.
void main():
    Callable[int(int)] h = (int x): x + 1
    Option[Callable[int(int)]] o = Some(^h)
    match o:
        case Some(f):
            print(f(1))
        else:
            print(0)
    Callable[int(int)] p = (int x): x + 1
    Vector[Callable[int(int)]] fs = []
    fs.push(^p)
    print(fs[0](1))
